QUESTION 3 - LAYERS OF ABSTRACTION IN COMPUTER SYSTEMS
ANSWER - ABSTRACTION IS REMOVAL OF UNNECESSARY DETAIL. COMPUTER SYSTEMS ARE ORGANISED INTO LAYERS AND EACH LAYER USES THE SERVICES BELOW IT
LAYER 1 - APPLICATIONS - USERS INTERACT WITH APPLICATIONS
LAYER 2- HIGH LEVEL LANGUAGES - THEY USED TO EXPRESS ALGORITHMS WITHOUT SPEIFYING INDIVIDUAL CPU INSTRUCTIONS.
LAYER 3 - OPERATING SYSTEMS - IT PROVIDES SERVICES FOR MANAGING PROCESSES, MEMORY, FILES AND DEVICES
LAYER 4 - INSTRUCTION SET ARCHITECTURE - IT PROVIDES MACHINE INSTRUCTIONS , REGISTERS AND OPERATIONS WHICH ARE AVAILABLE TO THE SOFTWARE
LAYER 5 - MICROARCHITECTURE - IT PROVIDES THE HARDWARE THAT IMPLEMENTS THOSE INSTRUCTIONS INCLUDING DATAPATHS AND CONTROL CIRCUITS
LAYERS 6 -  DIGITAL LOGIC - IT PROVIDES GATES AND CIRCUITS THAT PROCESS AND STORE BINARY VALUES
LAYER 7 - ELECTRONIC DEVICES - IT PROVIDES TRANSISTORS THAT PHYSICALLY IMPLEMENTS THE CIRCUITS
